# What a published package does not need.
#
# This is the tarball's list, not git's: a registry publish (npm pack, upm-ci)
# reads it, and installing straight from the git URL does not — that clones the
# repository as it stands. So it is one of two halves. The other is the
# UNITY_INCLUDE_TESTS constraint on OneText.Editor.Dev and the test assemblies,
# which is what keeps the golden-image harness, the benchmarks and the proof
# generators from compiling into a project that installed this from anywhere at
# all.
#
# Samples~ stays: package.json declares it, and the Package Manager offers it as
# an import. README, CHANGELOG, LICENSE and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES stay, because
# the Package Manager shows them.

# The test suite and its fixtures — 27 MB, none of it compiled in a project
# that has not asked to run our tests.
Tests/

# Editor tooling that only this repository runs: golden images, benchmarks,
# the proof-image generators, the native plugin importer batch.
Editor/Dev/
Editor/Onboarding/Tmp/Dev/

# The site, the wasm harness and the developer docs.
page~/
Web~/
Docs/
Documentation~/

# Build and maintenance scripts, and the smoke-test projects they drive.
Tools/

# Repository furniture.
.github/
.claude/
.omx/
CONTRIBUTING.md

# The .meta files of the folders above. Unity generates one per folder and they
# are tracked, so excluding a folder leaves its meta behind pointing at nothing.
Tests.meta
Docs.meta
Tools.meta
Dev.meta
CONTRIBUTING.md.meta
